From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:20:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] feat(proxy): take rule secrets from lease credentials
 and renew them

A `[[proxy.rules]]` entry can now name a credential from one of the active
profile's leases, so short-lived tokens can be brokered through
`fnox proxy run` without being stored as secrets. Names resolve as in
`fnox exec`: a lease credential wins over a same-name secret, and a later
lease wins over an earlier one. Only leases that may supply a rule run:
those that declare a rule name, and `command` leases.

While the command runs, fnox renews each injected lease credential before
the lease expires and swaps the new value in under the same placeholder.
Replaced values stay redacted from responses for the rest of the session.

